# Runtime pack pins (Phase 2.2.2, D-03): ONE Python 3.12.15 interpreter holding venv A + the Basic Pitch set.
# Merge rule: every name==version pin of requirements-a.txt, plus the venv-B-only names
# (requirements-b.txt names absent from requirements-a.txt). Shared names keep the venv-A version
# (librosa 1.0.0, numpy 2.5.3, scipy 1.18.1, scikit-learn 1.9.1, ...), except setuptools, which is
# forced to the venv-B pin 80.10.2 because resampy 0.4.2 imports pkg_resources (02.1 Pitfall 7).
# No tensorflow / tflite / coremltools: basic-pitch 0.4.0 picks its backend at import time and, with
# onnxruntime present and tensorflow absent, loads saved_models/icassp_2022/nmp.onnx.
# basic-pitch's install-time markers would pull tensorflow on 3.11+, so the whole set is installed
# with --no-deps --require-hashes from requirements-pack.txt (generated from this file, see its header).
# No new packages: every name was approved in the 02.1 Package Legitimacy Audit.
#
# --- venv A pins (requirements-a.txt; setuptools replaced by the venv B pin) ---
